Disable the glibc compatibility layer on non-Linux systems.

MIU Darwin has its own C library (libmiu, shipped as /usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib)
and provides no glibc symbol versioning, so force_link_glibc_2.17.h must not be
included.  Without this the build fails while compiling the agent.

Note on host_machine vs target_machine: in meson, target_machine only has a
meaning when the thing being built is itself a compiler.  For an ordinary
application, the machine the code will run on is host_machine.  MIU Darwin is
cross compiled from Fedora, so the two genuinely differ here and the condition
has to be written against host_machine.

--- agent/meson.build.orig
+++ agent/meson.build
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@

 if get_option('libc-compat')
 libc_compat = true
-if target_machine.cpu_family() == 'x86_64'
+if target_machine.cpu_family() == 'x86_64' and host_machine.system() == 'linux'
   ptyxis_agent_c_args += ['-include', 'x86_64/force_link_glibc_2.17.h']
 else
   libc_compat = false
